I added the `claude` provider. Typecheck, lint and the full test suite pass (63 tests, including 9 new ones in `claude.test.ts` and one new CLI test). You still need to run the real-login smoke test with your actual Claude Code login; nothing has been tried against the real CLI yet. I checked the flag names against `claude --help` on this machine.

**What changed:**
- **`src/providers/claude.ts`** (new): runs `claude -p <prompt> --dangerously-skip-permissions --output-format stream-json --verbose`, adding `--model <m>` when a model is given and any extra flags from `GRAPH_EXECUTION_CLAUDE_ARGS`. The arguments are passed as one list, never through a shell. It runs in the worktree with stdin closed, and aborting the signal kills it.
  - Each line of output becomes an output event: the assistant's text when there is some, otherwise the raw line. An exit event comes last.
  - Error messages (stderr) are passed through as raw lines too, so things like "not logged in" show up in the logs.
  - A comment block at the top of the file describes the pattern (args builder, line parser, registry entry) for the Codex and OpenCode adapters.
- **`src/providers/spawn.ts`**: if the process can't start at all (e.g. the CLI isn't installed), `done` now rejects with `failed to start "claude": …` instead of reporting exit code 1. It also merges stdout and stderr so the adapter can read both.
- **`src/providers/index.ts`**: `getProvider("claude")` first runs `which claude`. If that fails, the run stops at startup with exit 2 and the message `the "claude" CLI was not found on the PATH; install it and log in before running`. `fake` still works, and `codex`/`opencode` still say "not implemented yet". `startup.ts` now passes the repo as the working directory for this check.
- **Tests**:
  - `claude.test.ts` puts a small fake `claude` script on PATH. It checks the exact arguments, the working directory, the event stream, `--model` and the extra flags from the env var, a non-zero exit code, that aborting kills the process, the "can't start" error, and the PATH check.
  - `cli.test.ts` has a new end-to-end test: `--provider claude` with no `claude` on PATH exits 2.

No API keys or credentials are read, set or logged; the CLI uses your existing login. Nothing is committed.
